<----------------------------------------------------BIG theta notation----------------------------------------------------->

In simple language, Big - Theta(Θ) notation specifies asymptotic bounds (both upper and lower) for a function f(n) and provides the tightest bound for the growth rate of the function.
It is used to describe the average-case time complexity of an algorithm, indicating that the algorithm's running time grows at a rate that is both upper and lower bounded by a specific function.


